    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhile developing an LSP server, I ran into what looks like an ambiguity in how Neovim handles diagnostics when a server uses both:\n\n- `textDocument/publishDiagnostics`\n- `textDocument/diagnostic` / `workspace/diagnostic`\n\nfor the same client/buffer.\n\nIf the server pushes a fast native diagnostic first, and later the same diagnostic is returned through the pull path, Neovim appears to keep both and show duplicate diagnostics to the user.\n\n### Reproduction shape\n\nThe server behavior was roughly:\n\n1. Client supports pull diagnostics\n2. Server computes a fast native diagnostic\n3. Server sends it via `publishDiagnostics`\n4. Server also caches diagnostics for pull\n5. Client later pulls via `textDocument/diagnostic`\n6. The same diagnostic is returned again\n7. Neovim displays both copies\n\nIn our case this showed up as duplicated namespace/class mismatch diagnostics with identical:\n\n- range\n- severity\n- source\n- code\n- message\n\n### What I found\n\nWhile digging through Neovim’s source, it looks like push and pull diagnostics are tracked in separate namespaces and then combined, rather than deduplicated.\n\nThat makes sense structurally, but it means a server trying to do:\n\n- push for fast diagnostics\n- pull for the eventual full set\n\ncan easily produce duplicate visible diagnostics if the same item exists in both channels.\n\n### Questions\n\n1. Is this expected behavior in Neovim?\n2. Is the intended recommendation that servers should choose one native-diagnostic transport per client:\n   - push-only for push clients\n   - pull-only for pull-capable clients\n3. Would Neovim be open to deduplicating *exactly identical* diagnostics when merging push and pull results for the same client/buffer?\n\nBy “exactly identical”, I mean same:\n- line/column range\n- severity\n- source\n- code\n- message\n\nI’m not suggesting fuzzy deduplication, only collapsing exact duplicates that likely came from the same server through both transports.\n\n### Why this matters\n\nFor server authors, “push fast, pull full” is an appealing design:\n- fast feedback immediately\n- slower diagnostics later\n- good UX in theory\n\nBut if clients surface both copies, it becomes difficult to use both transports together safely.\n\nIn the end I changed the server to use **pull-only for native diagnostics** when the client supports pull, and that avoided the duplicate display. That works, but it would be helpful to know whether that is the intended/expected model from Neovim’s perspective.\n\n### Environment\n\n- Neovim: `NVIM v0.13.0-dev-1012+ga297985d05`\n- Built from latest `master`\n- LSP server: custom server under development\n- Observed with pull diagnostics enabled\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
