            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I dug into this further from the server side and wanted to sanity-check the intended client/server contract here.\n\nFor context, I was able to avoid the problem in my LSP by changing the server behavior to:\n\n- if the client is push-only: use `publishDiagnostics`\n- if the client supports pull diagnostics: use `textDocument/diagnostic` / `workspace/diagnostic` as the only native-diagnostics channel\n\nThat fixes the duplicate display in Neovim.\n\nWhat I’m trying to understand is whether that is actually the *recommended* model from Neovim’s perspective, or just a pragmatic workaround.\n\n## What I found\n\nMy original server behavior was:\n\n1. compute fast native diagnostics\n2. send them with `publishDiagnostics`\n3. later expose the full native set through pull diagnostics\n\nThat is attractive from a UX standpoint because fast diagnostics show up immediately, and slower ones arrive later.\n\nBut in Neovim, the same diagnostic coming from:\n- push namespace\n- pull namespace\n\nends up being displayed twice.\n\nI also tried a client-side dedupe approach locally: when pull diagnostics arrive, remove exact duplicates from the push namespace. That fixes the steady-state duplicate, but not the transient flicker:\n\n- first the pushed diagnostic appears\n- then both show briefly\n- then it settles back to one\n\nSo deduping *after* both channels have already rendered does not fully solve the UX problem.\n\n## Question\n\nWould you consider it the intended model that if a client supports pull diagnostics, servers should generally avoid pushing the same native diagnostics?\n\nOr put differently:\n\n- should clients be expected to handle “push fast / pull full” cleanly?\n- or is the expected/recommended server behavior really “pick one transport per client”?\n\n## Why I’m asking\n\nOther editors seem to tolerate this mixed model better, so I want to understand whether:\n\n1. Neovim should eventually normalize/dedupe exact push+pull duplicates\n2. or whether mixed push/pull for the same native diagnostics is just not something clients should be expected to support well\n\nFrom my side, I can keep the server on:\n- push-only for push clients\n- pull-only for pull-capable clients\nas it works\n\nI just want to make sure that’s the right long-term direction, rather than papering over something Neovim would prefer to handle on its side.\n",
