            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The server sending the same diagnostics via push, and pull and then having the client deduplicate them sounds pretty backward to me (\"von hinten durch die Brust ins Auge\").\n\nThe spec also mentions:\n\n> When a file changes, it is the server’s responsibility to re-compute diagnostics and push them to the client. If the computed set is empty, the server has to push the empty array to clear former diagnostics. Newly pushed diagnostics always replace previously pushed diagnostics. *There is no merging that happens on the client side*.\n\nAlthough given that this is only in the publishDiagnostic section, it's not clear whether that is for all of the diagnostics.\n\nBut pull also has:\n\n```\n\t/**\n\t * An optional identifier under which the diagnostics are\n\t * managed by the client.\n\t */\n\tidentifier?: string;\n```\n\nI guess one thing we could do is ask for clarification if no identifier means it should get merged into the push namespace. But given that push says no merging should happen, it would then need simply override all - with no property based deduplication.\n\n",
