        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "See comment https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40781#issuecomment-5003613081 (trying to keep conversation on PR lol)\n\n> I guess one thing we could do is ask for clarification if no identifier means it should get merged into the push namespace. But given that push says no merging should happen, it would then need simply override all - with no property based deduplication.\n\nPush is the legacy system that Pull was designed to replace---**pull should never be merged into push**.\n\n> the intent is to push diagnostice each time another one finishes, it's not the intend to have the client merge them, the server would do so and send the full set each time\n\nPull is the system designed to replace push---so push should only be used as a fallback if the client does not support pull. Sending everything down all at once is the exact thing the pull system was designed to prevent\n",
            "created_at": "2026-07-17T13:28:36Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40774#issuecomment-5003771666",
            "id": 5003771666,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/40774",
