        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Then merging them together sounds like wallpapering over a misbehaving server?\n\nI would think so, but I'm sure others have a different viewpoint. I'm just trying to make this more robust to improve UX when a server uses both and sends down duplicate diagnostics via both channels. As mentioned on #29927, \"both vscode and helix seem to handle this without issues\"",
